Input: {"question": "Which award did Philip Proctor receive?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": "Philip Proctor"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 16, "end": 210, "text": "Philip Proctor (born 1942) is a New Zealand industrialist and entrepreneur, best known for his contributions to the development of sustainable manufacturing practices in the Asia-Pacific region."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 211, "end": 235, "text": "Early Life and Education"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 237, "end": 308, "text": "Proctor was born in Auckland, New Zealand, to a family of modest means."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 309, "end": 475, "text": "He demonstrated a keen interest in science and technology from an early age, and went on to pursue a degree in mechanical engineering from the University of Auckland."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 476, "end": 643, "text": "After completing his studies, Proctor worked for several years in the manufacturing sector, where he developed a passion for innovative design and process improvement."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 644, "end": 650, "text": "Career"}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 652, "end": 783, "text": "In the 1980s, Proctor founded Proctor Industries, a company that specialized in the production of eco-friendly packaging materials."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 784, "end": 908, "text": "Under his leadership, the company grew rapidly, and Proctor became a respected figure in the New Zealand business community."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 909, "end": 1093, "text": "In the 1990s, Proctor expanded his operations to include sustainable energy solutions, and his company became a leading provider of renewable energy systems in the Asia-Pacific region."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1094, "end": 1251, "text": "His commitment to environmental sustainability earned him numerous awards and recognition, including the prestigious Austrian Decoration for Science and Art."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1252, "end": 1291, "text": "Austrian Decoration for Science and Art"}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1293, "end": 1495, "text": "The Austrian Decoration for Science and Art is a prestigious award conferred by the Austrian government to individuals who have made significant contributions to the fields of science, art, and culture."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1496, "end": 1610, "text": "The award was established in 1957 and is considered one of the highest honors bestowed by the Austrian government."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1611, "end": 1772, "text": "In 2001, Proctor was awarded the Austrian Decoration for Science and Art in recognition of his pioneering work in sustainable manufacturing and renewable energy."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1773, "end": 1850, "text": "The award was presented to him by the Austrian Ambassador to New Zealand, Dr."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1851, "end": 1894, "text": "Helmut Tichy, at a ceremony held in Vienna."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1895, "end": 1917, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1919, "end": 2028, "text": "* \"Sustainable Manufacturing Practices in the Asia-Pacific Region: A Case Study of Proctor Industries\" by Dr."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2029, "end": 2083, "text": "Maria Rodriguez, Journal of Sustainable Business, Vol."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2084, "end": 2091, "text": "12, No."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2092, "end": 2100, "text": "3, 2005."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2101, "end": 2177, "text": "* \"Renewable Energy Systems in New Zealand: A Review of the Industry\" by Dr."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2178, "end": 2210, "text": "John Taylor, Energy Policy, Vol."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2211, "end": 2218, "text": "35, No."}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2219, "end": 2228, "text": "10, 2007."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2229, "end": 2290, "text": "* \"Austrian Decoration for Science and Art: A History\" by Dr."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2291, "end": 2343, "text": "Elisabeth Steininger, Austrian Cultural Forum, 2010."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 69, "text": "Title: The Industrialist's Honor: Philip Proctor's Rise to Knighthood"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 71, "end": 309, "text": "In the early 20th century, New Zealand was undergoing a period of rapid industrialization, and at the forefront of this transformation was Philip Proctor, a visionary entrepreneur who would leave an indelible mark on the nation's economy."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 310, "end": 514, "text": "Born and raised in Auckland, Proctor's innate business acumen and innovative spirit drove him to establish a series of successful ventures, cementing his reputation as a leading industrialist of his time."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 515, "end": 566, "text": "As Proctor's empire expanded, so did his influence."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 567, "end": 687, "text": "He became a respected voice in the business community, known for his progressive ideas and commitment to social welfare."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 688, "end": 928, "text": "His dedication to the betterment of New Zealand's industrial landscape did not go unnoticed, and in 1923, he was recognized for his outstanding contributions with the prestigious award of Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 929, "end": 1099, "text": "This esteemed honor, conferred upon Proctor by King George V, was a testament to his tireless efforts in promoting the growth and development of New Zealand's industries."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1100, "end": 1309, "text": "The Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire, a rank within the Order of the British Empire, is one of the highest honors bestowed upon individuals for their exceptional service to the Commonwealth."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1310, "end": 1414, "text": "Proctor's remarkable journey to knighthood was paved by his pioneering work in the manufacturing sector."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1415, "end": 1571, "text": "In the early 1900s, he founded the Proctor Manufacturing Company, which quickly became a leading producer of textiles, machinery, and other essential goods."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1572, "end": 1728, "text": "His innovative approach to production, which emphasized efficiency, quality, and worker welfare, set a new standard for industrial practices in New Zealand."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1729, "end": 1815, "text": "As his business empire expanded, Proctor's philanthropic efforts also gained momentum."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1816, "end": 1979, "text": "He was a vocal advocate for workers' rights, and his companies were known for providing fair wages, safe working conditions, and opportunities for social mobility."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1980, "end": 2140, "text": "His commitment to the well-being of his employees earned him widespread respect and admiration, both within the business community and among the general public."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2141, "end": 2269, "text": "Proctor's contributions to New Zealand's war effort during World War I further solidified his reputation as a dedicated patriot."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2270, "end": 2423, "text": "He played a crucial role in mobilizing the nation's industrial resources, ensuring a steady supply of essential goods and materials to the Allied forces."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2424, "end": 2604, "text": "His selfless dedication to the war effort did not go unnoticed, and in 1918, he was appointed an Officer of the Order of the British Empire, a precursor to his eventual knighthood."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Philip Proctor", "scope": "1923", "claim": "Philip Proctor received the Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire in 1923.", "answer": "Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire", "quote": "His dedication to the betterment of New Zealand's industrial landscape did not go unnoticed, and in 1923, he was recognized for his outstanding contributions with the prestigious award of Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire. This esteemed honor, conferred upon Proctor by King George V, was a testament to his tireless efforts in promoting the growth and development of New Zealand's industries. The Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire, a rank within the Order of the British Empire, is one of the highest honors bestowed upon individuals for their exceptional service to the Commonwealth.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["Austrian Decoration for Science and Art", "Knight Commander of the Order of the British Empire"]}
